{
 "id": "grafana-alerting",
 "title": "Build the on-call dashboard and alert in Grafana",
 "kind": "tool",
 "tool": "Grafana + Prometheus",
 "minutes": 25,
 "skill_ids": [
  "promql",
  "dashboards",
  "alerting"
 ],
 "briefing": "Your team just installed Prometheus, but nobody can see anything yet. In this **simulated Grafana** you will:\n\n1. Connect the **Prometheus data source** (it runs at `http://prometheus:9090`).\n2. Use **Explore** to write the PromQL queries an on-call engineer needs.\n3. Create an **alert rule** that pages when the 5xx error rate stays above 5% for 5 minutes.\n\nOpen *Grafana (simulated)* in the Apps tab. Everything behaves like the real tool's workflow: Connections → Data sources, Explore, Alerting → Alert rules.",
